tie ports a small set of Metal compute kernels. Everything else in tie is original.

From llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), commit 9c2e0e491a822adae1f0b1c831adb4160057d24f:
  src/kernels/metal/common.h        <- ggml-metal/kernels/common.h, dequantize.h; ggml-common.h (block_q8_0)
  src/kernels/metal/ggml_args.h     <- ggml-metal/ggml-metal-impl.h (argument structs)
  src/kernels/metal/elementwise.metal <- ggml-metal/kernels/quantize.metal (get_rows), unary.metal (swiglu)
  src/kernels/metal/rope.metal      <- ggml-metal/kernels/rope.metal (rope_neox; YaRN helpers
                                       MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2023 Jeffrey Quesnelle and Bowen Peng)
                                       tie changes: precise::cos/sin in rope_yarn; the angle uses a
                                       host-computed inv_freq table (HF formula) passed in the
                                       freq-factor slot instead of pow(freq_base, ...)
  src/kernels/metal/mul_mv.metal    <- ggml-metal/kernels/mul_mv.metal (t_t_4 and q8_0 matvec)
  src/kernels/metal/mul_mm.metal    <- ggml-metal/kernels/mul_mm.metal (simdgroup matmul; BF16 instance
                                       changed to half staging)

